@startuml poll-merge
' cumin works - the approved pull request (start the merge, ask for the merge decision) and the steps in cumin/status/merging.
' Document: poll.md, section on the merge step.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

start
:The Reviewer approved the head commit;
:Read the issue of the run again
and the required checks;
if (Exactly one risk/* label
on the issue? (DecideMerge)) then (no)
  :Stop step of #81, stop the review
  (no or two risk labels);
  stop
elseif (Required checks pass
on the head commit?) then (no)
  :Back to cumin/status/checking;
  stop
elseif (risk/low?) then (no)
  :ask for the merge decision: cumin/status/awaiting-merge-decision,
  then cumin-core requests the review of the Issue Owner
  (requested_reviewers; a failure is only logged),
  then one notification with the pull request;
  stop
else (yes)
  :start the merge: cumin/status/merging
  (only the label changes; start the merge does the same
  after the approval of a Maintainer);
endif
partition "At every poll, for an issue in cumin/status/merging" {
  :Read the issue again: the actor of the label,
  the pull request, the reviews, the checks,
  the permissions, and the required checks;
  if (cumin-core or a Maintainer
added the label?) then (no)
    :Do nothing;
    stop
  endif
  if (An open pull request?) then (no)
    if (The newest linked pull request
is merged?) then (yes)
      :Close the merged issue:
      cumin-core closes it as completed
      when GitHub left it open
      (a lasting failure: stop the merge);
    else (no)
      :Go back to the checks:
      cumin/status/checking;
    endif
    stop
  endif
  if (The conditions of the merge hold?
(MergeConditionsHold)) then (no)
    :Go back to the checks:
    cumin/status/checking, no merge;
    stop
  endif
  if (GitHub reports a conflict?
(mergeable is CONFLICTING)) then (yes)
    :No merge is sent;
    :Request a conflict resolution:
    wait for the permit of the start, then
    cumin/status/implementing, then the Implementer
    resolves it in the same session;
    stop
  endif
  :Wait 5 seconds after an earlier merge of this poll.
  cumin-core merges with merge_method
  and sha = the approved head commit;
  if (Merged, a lost answer, a temporary failure,
or 405 "Base branch was modified"?) then (yes)
    :Keep cumin/status/merging, no comment.
    The next poll reads the pull request again;
  elseif (Conflict? (405, mergeable false)) then (yes)
    :Request a conflict resolution:
    wait for the permit of the start, then
    cumin/status/implementing, then the Implementer
    resolves it in the same session;
  else (no)
    :Stop the merge:
    cumin/status/awaiting-decision, head moved (409),
    or the answer of GitHub;
  endif
}
stop
@enduml
